    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The structure of W-questions",
     "texto": [
      "In a question with a question word (W-Frage), the order is fixed and very clear:",
      "**Position 1:** the question word (**Wie** = how, in what way).",
      "**Position 2:** the conjugated verb (**heißt, heißen, geht, ist, schreibt, buchstabiert**).",
      "**Position 3:** the subject (**du, Sie, es, man**).",
      "Everyday examples:",
      "**Wie heißt du?** (what is your name?) → Position 1: Wie | Position 2: heißt | Position 3: du",
      "**Wie geht es dir?** (how are you?) → Position 1: Wie | Position 2: geht | Position 3: es",
      "**Wie schreibt man das?** (how do you spell that?) → Position 1: Wie | Position 2: schreibt | Position 3: man",
      "Remember: in an affirmative answer, the conjugated verb also stays in **position 2**: **Ich heiße Jonas.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
